        "en": "How Hangul Syllables Work",
        "ko": "한글 음절 조합 원리"
      },
      "text": "Every Korean syllable block has at least one consonant and one vowel: Initial consonant + Vowel (e.g., ㄱ + ㅏ = 가, ㅇ + ㅗ = 오). Many blocks add a final consonant (받침) at the bottom: Initial + Vowel + Final (e.g., ㄱ + ㅏ + ㄴ = 간, ㅂ + ㅏ + ㅂ = 밥)."
    },
